\fs36\b Strikethrough (T1.1)\b0\fs24\par
This is \strike deleted text\strike0  inside a sentence.\par
\strike Whole line struck through.\strike0 \par
Mixed \b bold and \strike struck\strike0  together\b0 .\par
\fs36\b Reference links, titles, images (T1.2)\b0\fs24\par
Inline link with title: Anthropic (https://www.anthropic.com).\par
Reference link: the docs (https://example.com/docs) explain more.\par
Collapsed reference: Docs Ref (https://example.com/docs-ref) also works.\par
Shortcut reference: Docs Ref (https://example.com/docs-ref) resolves the same way.\par
Undefined reference stays literal: [nowhere][missing-ref].\par
Undefined shortcut stays literal: [Also Missing].\par
Image with title: [image: a small logo] (https://example.com/logo.png)\par
Reference image: [image: alt text] (https://example.com/image.png)\par
Paren url survives inline: Haskell (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haskell_(programming_language)) stays whole.\par
Paren url by reference: the Haskell article (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haskell_(programming_language)).\par
Paren-form title: point here (https://example.com/pt) uses (title) syntax.\par
\fs36\b Math small fixes (T1.5)\b0\fs24\par
Cube root: \u8731?(8). Fourth root: \u8732?(16). Other index: [5]\u8730?(32).\par
Plain root unaffected: \u8730?2.\par
Nested content under a cube root: \u8731?(x+y).\par
